* cdl_tail.cdl -- the LAST file of every LVS reference netlist (PAD_CDLS).
*
* Nothing in it but comments. LibreLane 3.0.16's KLayout.LVS concatenates the
* design CDL, CELL_CDLS, EXTRA_CDLS and PAD_CDLS into a NamedTemporaryFile and
* starts KLayout without flushing it, so up to the last 8 KiB (Python's write
* buffer) never reach the disk. With the PDK's pad CDL last, that truncated
* the pad library -- unused here, and harmless only as long as the cut fell
* between two lines -- on sg13cmos5l it did not ("Can't find a value for a R,
* C or L device", "Pin count mismatch"). With a short file last, it truncated
* custom_stdcell.cdl and custom_cap_4 vanished from the reference.
*
* These macros contain no pads, so PAD_CDLS is this file alone, and it is
* longer than the buffer: what is lost is padding.
*
